url: https://www.standuppouches.net/blog/what-materials-are-juice-pouches-made-of

The harder case. A [[Tetra Pak]] carton is mostly paper. A pouch has no paper in it at all.

<<<
These films are laminated together to make a multiple layer structure that protects juices from oxidation
<<< [[standuppouches.net|https://www.standuppouches.net/blog/what-materials-are-juice-pouches-made-of]]

Plastic film on plastic film, with [[Aluminum]] foil in the middle to keep out the sun. It can be made tough enough to survive a lunchbox.

Nothing in it can be soaked loose. Curbside recycling doesn't take them.

See [[Monstrous Hybrid]], [[Plasticshed]]
